 - **Execution controls:** separate pilot configuration/approval binds identity, hash, host, rights and validity. Default command is plan-only; shipped template approved=false. Approval hash durable before intake. No self-approval implied by code. Offline recovery remains possible after a connection permit expires. SIGINT/SIGTERM stop intake; explicit outer watchdog covers OS DNS/unresponsive-process limits. Journal charge and bounded artifacts are not a filesystem quota or 24/7 certification.
 - **Evidence:** 127 final focused checks pass; earlier backend regression passed 311 before six further focused cases/fixes. Mypy over 45 source files and scoped Ruff pass; both typing failures and correction diffs preserved. No altered behavioral expectations. Scientific/core/history evidence unchanged. Earlier native campaigns not rerun; no real observations or financial metrics generated.
 - **Readiness:** no material implementation blocker identified within simulated scope; prepared to request a separately approved 5–10 minute pilot. Before execution bind retention rights, host clock/storage, optional runtime and watchdog. Actual TLS/subscriptions/traffic/latency are pilot questions, not claims already verified. Limits can stop before target duration; valid prefix QA alone cannot count as a completed pilot. E3/E4, 26 specifications, C1/C3, C2, C4/C5, T/D/U/V/F, holdout and V/paper/live unchanged.
+
+
+## D-061 — Authorized finite public Kraken pilot
+
+- **Date/authority:** 2026-11-15. The user explicitly authorizes finishing Market Replay from `2316029`, full applicable regression and a supervised 5–10 minute public WebSocket v2 BTC/EUR trade+ticker/BBO capture. No additional approval is required within that scope. This supersedes D-060’s historical no-connection condition only for this finite private technical pilot.
+- **Execution binding:** reuse `PilotConfiguration`/`PilotApproval`, actual host and finite time window; record the user's instruction as authority, not an invented external verification. Public information is retained privately for technical QA; no market messages, extracts or normalized data will be redistributed. Existing source/rights restrictions remain; no new general licensing research.
+- **Boundaries:** five-minute intake target with existing journal/row/artifact limits, external supervision, four CPU/eight GiB RSS ceiling and 512 MiB fresh temporary budget. No new engine, paid service, financial experiment or permanent collector. Preserve failures and rerun only affected tests. E3/E4 economics, 26 specifications, scientific gates/holdout and Phase V/paper/live remain unchanged.
+- **Status at registration:** authorized, not yet executed. Results will be recorded separately without rewriting this entry. Stop after delivery; next objective is E3/E4.
